# rule.forbid.nonidempotent-mutations

mutations (db, api, filesystem — dao methods, domain operations, endpoints) use only idempotent verbs, safe on retry:
- findsert — find extant or insert; retry returns extant
- upsert — update or insert; retry overwrites
- delete — remove if extant; retry is a no-op
forbidden: create, insert, add (duplicate on retry) · save, update (ambiguous)
daos: `findByUnique`, `findsert`, `upsert`, `deleteByUnique`
```ts
export const findsertTask = async (input: { exid: string }, context: { daoTask: DaoTask }) => {
  const taskFound = await context.daoTask.findByUnique({ exid: input.exid });
  if (taskFound) return taskFound;
  return context.daoTask.insert(input);
};
```
exception: in-memory setters
enforcement: create*, insert*, add*, save* mutations = blocker; ambiguous update* = blocker
